Mesa 26.2.6 for the Radeon RX 550 on big-endian PowerPC (Power Mac G5) - Arch POWER
====================================================================================

These packages replace Arch POWER's Mesa packages (ppc64, big-endian, ELFv2). Each one provides
and conflicts with the Arch package of the same base name, so pacman asks to replace it:

  mesa-rx550g5                 mesa (Gallium: radeonsi, r300, r600, nouveau, virgl, zink,
                               llvmpipe, softpipe; GL, EGL, GLX, GBM, VA-API)
  vulkan-radeon-rx550g5        vulkan-radeon (RADV)
  vulkan-swrast-rx550g5        vulkan-swrast (lavapipe)
  vulkan-mesa-layers-rx550g5   vulkan-mesa-layers + vulkan-mesa-implicit-layers
  opencl-mesa-rx550g5          opencl-mesa (Rusticl on radeonsi)

The source is the same commit as the Debian/MintPPC release 26.2.6-1+rx550g5.3 (branch g5-26 of
mesa-rx550-be, which includes Debian's three Mesa patches), plus four Arch fixes:
  0001  build fix for glibc 2.44's native C11 threads (pointer casts only)
  0002  RADV: report the kernel page size as minImportedHostPointerAlignment
        (VK_EXT_external_memory_host imports failed with 64 KiB pages)
  0003  RADV: align sparse images to at least the CPU page size (4 KiB sparse
        binds became overlapping 64 KiB mappings with 64 KiB pages)
  0004  EGL/Wayland: use DRM byte-layout formats for 8-bit RGB visuals on
        big-endian (every Wayland EGL client crashed in eglSwapBuffers)
0002, 0003 and 0004 change nothing on little-endian hosts or with 4 KiB pages.
They use Arch POWER's llvm-libs 22, clang, libclc and
spirv-llvm-translator.

OpenCL notes
------------
* Rusticl is enabled on radeonsi by default here (upstream and Debian need
  RUSTICL_ENABLE=radeonsi). clinfo shows "rusticl" with the RX 550.
* The device reports itself as big-endian (CL_DEVICE_ENDIAN_LITTLE = false):
  buffers, kernel arguments and images hold host-order data, as OpenCL
  requires. Atomics on buffers run as compare-and-swap loops.
* fp64 (cl_khr_fp64) is off by default, as upstream; RUSTICL_FEATURES=fp64
  turns it on.
* The first build of a program takes about 10 seconds on a PPC970MP (clang and
  libclc); later builds of the same source come from the shader cache in about
  a second. Driver updates empty that cache.

What changed compared with stock Mesa 26.2.6
--------------------------------------------
The full source diff is rx550-g5-vs-mesa-26.2.6.diff.gz in this directory
(it includes the three Debian patches and the four Arch fixes). Almost all of it only takes effect on
a big-endian CPU with a GFX8 GPU (Polaris: RX 460/470/480/550/560/570/580);
other GPUs and CPUs get stock code.

* GPU commands: command buffers, fences, shader binaries, descriptors and
  query results are converted to the GPU's little-endian byte order. UVD
  decode messages are encoded little-endian.
* Application data: vertex and index buffers, texel and image buffers, SSBOs,
  buffer device addresses, clears and copies between buffers and images are
  converted in the driver or in the shader.
* On big-endian, radeonsi compiles shaders with LLVM; RADV uses ACO.
* Shared Mesa code that was wrong on big-endian: HTILE (depth compression)
  bitfields, packed-float formats, DRI/EGL framebuffer formats, Vulkan vertex
  binding strides, the sparse-buffer PRT workaround bit read from libdrm, and
  VA-API P010/P016 images (kept little-endian, as VA-API defines them).
* RADV reports Vulkan 1.3 on this configuration (the tested CTS is 1.3).
* OpenCL: SPIR-V and clang output on a big-endian host, libclc NIR
  serialisation, kernel memory byte order. Two fixes are not big-endian
  specific: scratch (private memory) accesses now carry their real alignment
  in the LLVM backend, and image copies on compute-only contexts discard DCC
  first so that float NaN payloads are copied bit for bit.

Testing
-------
The Debian release built from this source was tested on a Power Mac G5 with an RX 550: Khronos
GL CTS (17,887 cases), a stratified Vulkan CTS sample (63,560 cases), VA-API decode, VCE encode
and the OpenCL CTS quick list. This Arch POWER build (GCC 16, ELFv2, 64 KiB pages) was tested on a Power Mac G5 Quad with an
RX 550: GL/GLES CTS, Vulkan CTS sample, VA-API and OpenCL. Results: docs/STATUS.md in
https://github.com/parabellum-push/rx550-g5 (section "Arch POWER").

This is not a Khronos conformance submission.

These packages need the patched amdgpu kernel driver from linux-ppc64-rx550g5; the stock
kernel driver lacks the big-endian fixes.
